TASK B3 – EXACT vs APPROXIMATE: Emergency Service Set Cover (8 Marks)
Programming Language: Python
1. Aim
To implement and compare two algorithms for the Emergency Service Set Cover Problem:
1. Exact Algorithm: Finds the minimum number of emergency service centres required to cover all zones.
2. Greedy Approximation Algorithm: Selects the centre that covers the largest number of currently uncovered zones at each step.
The main objective is to compare their correctness, search effort, performance and solution quality.
2. Problem Description
Imagine a city divided into several zones. Emergency services such as fire stations, hospitals and ambulance centres must cover all zones.

Each candidate centre can provide services to a particular group of zones.

Our objective is to select the minimum number of centres so that every zone receives emergency service coverage.

Example:
- Zones: Z1, Z2, Z3, Z4, Z5, Z6.
- Candidate centres: C1, C2, C3, C4.
- Each centre covers a particular set of zones.
- We must select the minimum number of centres to cover all six zones.








