Why did Greedy fail?
In the first step, greedy selected centre A because it covered four zones.

However, this decision was not the best overall choice.

If the algorithm had selected B and C, all six zones would have been covered using only two centres.

The greedy algorithm makes locally best decisions but does not always consider the globally optimal combination.

Conclusion: This counterexample proves that the greedy solution can be larger than the exact minimum solution.
